WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.501
-Standing ovation
for Kelsey Grammer.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.567
-Very nice.
My goodness.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.400
-Oh, my God.
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.234
Thanks for being here.
-Thanks, man.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.634
-I was asking you backstage if
you ever had a perm or anything,

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.734
and you go, "No."
-No, no perms for me.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.300
-Nope.
Never a perm.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.133
But then you gave me a picture,
and I didn't know --

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.367
-There is some evidence
of hair work in my life, yeah.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:19.868
[ Laughter ]
-Wow! Look at --

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Good-looking.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.868
That's a stud!

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.968
That's a stud right there.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.667
Real long hair.
What were you into?

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.334
-This is when I was
17 years old.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:31.300
I was a surfer back then.
But --

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.234
And I used to --
When I would drop in like this,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.767
I would feel the hair would
splash down on my back.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.801
-Really? That long?
-You drop it in so it's --

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.133
And then there'll be a lift,
and you drop in,

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.968
and then the water would just
flow down my back.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:47.234
And I thought,
"This is the best life ever."

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.801
-That's so cool.
Eventually you ended up

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.167
cutting your hair --
-Looking like this.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:58.300
-Later that same year.
What made you cut it?

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.801
-When I was in tenth grade,
I ran for the student council.

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.434
And we all gave a damn
back then.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.067
And we thought, "You know what?
Damn it.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.267
We're not gonna live by this
hair code crap anymore,"

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:07.934
in my high school
that I went to.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.901
And -- so, they agreed.
They said, "Yes, let's do that."

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.634
Then they hired a new principal
the next year.

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:17.167
So, my junior year, they said,
"Back to the hair code."

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:20.267
And we said,
"Damn it. We say no."

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.367
-Yeah, we want to be able
to grow -- hair freedom, yeah.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.701
-So, I went shopping for a wig.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.834
And I saw, in a wig store,
in one of the malls

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:32.367
in Fort Lauderdale,
a Jane Fonda wig.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.033
And I thought,
"Well, that should work."

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.200
It was kind of long, though,
so I thought,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.701
"Well, I'll just
cut the back of it off."

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.400
So I just cut the back off,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.033
and I shoved all that hair
underneath there.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.734
-Wait.
So it actually is a wig?

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:45.901
-It is a wig.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:48.200
And then --
-So you wore a wig to school?

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.767
-I would go like this.
Put my hair in a ponytail,

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.033
put it up on the top of my head,
and I'd go like this,

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.934
and I'd go like that,
and I'd pull it back down.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:54.267
And I thought, "If they're
willing to let me look

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.968
this stupid,
I'm willing to do it."

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.567
-That's the best.

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.701
Did everyone --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.200
Did everyone know it was a wig?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.434
-Everybody knew it was a wig,
yeah.

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.567
-They knew it was a wig.
-There were three of us --

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:08.033
Ronnie Powell,
Bob Collier, and me.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.501
-I love it.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.734
-Bob and Ronnie both quit
about halfway through,

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.701
but I stuck it out.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.000
-Good for you.
Jane Fonda wig.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.834
I love that story.
Before we get into the movie,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.467
can we talk about, right now,
you're shooting --

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:23.167
you're filming the reboot
of "Frasier."

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.334
-Yes.
-This is a big deal.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:25.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.434
And people
are talking about this.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:30.267
It's exciting.
Is it strange to revisit

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:32.567
a character that you haven't
played in 20 years?

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.501
-Well, it's funny.
People used to ask me years ago,

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.734
you know, "How have you kept
this character alive

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.033
for as long
as you have already?"

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:39.834
And I said, "Well, it's like
waking up in the morning.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:43.234
You know, life is interesting."
-Yeah.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:46.334
And so a character that sort of
walks hand in hand with you

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:49.834
through your lifetime
is equally interesting.

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:52.067
As long as you don't, like,
drop the ball.

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:53.834
As long
as you don't stop caring."

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.567
And so I never stopped caring.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:58.868
It was actually when Roseanne
got her show back on,

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.467
I thought to myself,
"Well, you know,

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:02.868
Frasier's kind of interesting."

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:04.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.367
"We could maybe play him again."
-Yeah, and then the rumor is

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.601
that he's moving back to Boston.
-Right.

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:10.133
He's going back to Boston.
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:12.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wait, wait, for a --

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:13.834
You gotta come back for that,
okay?

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.033
-Yeah.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.100
-I want to talk about
your new movie.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.901
It's called "Jesus Revolution."

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:20.567
-Well, you got two choices.
"Cocaine Bear"...

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.734
...or the living Christ.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.634
Which one you want to go with?

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.868
-Oh, my goodness.
I never thought of that. Yeah.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:33.901
-But surely, on February 24th...
-You've got options.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:37.234
-...everybody's gonna be happy.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:38.534
-You can make some choices.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:39.901
-There's something
for everybody.

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.601
-Theater A or theater B.
Yeah.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.400
Wow. Yeah.
Or make a whole day out of it.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.734
-Or the guy
that rose from the dead.

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:48.200
One or the other.
-What drew you to do this film?

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.968
-Well, the truth is,
I was having a sort of

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.300
a meditative evening
one night in my home.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.400
And I was up pretty late.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.000
It was about 3:00,
4:00 in the morning.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.901
And I started thinking, "I want
to do something worthwhile,

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:01.868
something that has a bigger
purpose than just me."

00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:04.501
And I was kind of
saying a prayer, I guess,

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:07.701
and the next morning,
the script lands on my door.

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:10.601
And I read it, and I said,
"Okay.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.434
That's it.
I'm doing this Jesus story."

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:13.868
-Yeah.
-It was pretty cool.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.567
-This script came to you.
I'm so excited.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.634
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Kelsey Grammer

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.467
in "Jesus Revolution."
Take a look at this.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.334
-You tell me right now
where my daughter is.

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:24.267
Jeanette!
-What?

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.234
Here.
-Who is this?

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:29.033
-It's Lonnie.
-Hi.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:32.868
-Hi.
Uh, would you mind just, uh...

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.234
stepping outside
for a minute, mister...?

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.834
-Not at all.
Frisbee, Lonnie Frisbee.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.300
-Frisbee.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.901
Thank you.
-Sugar, by any cha--

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.267
-What is going on?

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:46.901
-You said you wanted God
to send you a hippy.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.601
-I said that...

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.567
but I did not mean it.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Come on.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.267
That's how to do it right there.
Kelsey Grammer, everybody!

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:59.100
"Jesus Revolution"
hits theaters February 24th.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.801
Please come back whenever,
buddy.

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:01.934
You're the best.
Kelsey Grammer.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.801
We'll be right back.
Come on.

